Sideways 4 – Structural Range Tradability (Swing-Based)
Objective

Replace heuristic channel logic (v2) with a structurally grounded, swing-based sideways detector optimized for:

15m timeframe

Medium-width tradable ranges

Clear support/resistance ping-pong behavior

No structural trend progression

No micro-noise chop

This version builds on v1 (SidewaysConsistencyScoreCalculator) and enhances it using explicit swing structure.

1. Conceptual Definition

We define a tradable sideways range as:

Low net displacement (no drift)

Repeated oscillation between upper and lower boundary

Swings that travel most of the range

Stable containment (clustered highs and lows)

Alternating structure (no higher-high / lower-low progression)

Medium relative width (not too tight, not too wide)

This is NOT:

Accumulation before breakout

Compression triangle

Volatility spike regime

Micro chop

2. Algorithm Overview

We extend v1:

baseScore = (1 - NDR) * RSS * ODS


Then multiply by structural modifiers:

score = baseScore
        * SwingTravelEfficiency
        * BoundaryClarity
        * AlternationPurity
        * WidthPreference


All modifiers ∈ [0.6, 1.1] (soft influence, no hard killers).

3. Required Inputs

From existing implementation:

Close prices (30 candles)

Precomputed:

Net Displacement Ratio (NDR)

Range Stability Score (RSS)

Oscillation Density Score (ODS)

Local extrema list (already implemented in v1)

4. New Structural Components
4.1 Swing Travel Efficiency
Purpose

Eliminate micro-chop and weak oscillations.

Logic

For each swing pair:

low → next high

high → next low

Compute:

swingAmplitude = abs(high - low)


Let:

avgSwingAmplitude = mean(swingAmplitude)
totalRange = maxPrice - minPrice
travelRatio = avgSwingAmplitude / totalRange

Scoring
if travelRatio >= 0.7 → 1.1
if 0.5 – 0.7 → 1.0
if 0.3 – 0.5 → 0.85
if < 0.3 → 0.7


Rationale:
Tradable ranges require near full-box travel.

4.2 Boundary Clarity
Purpose

Reward clear support and resistance clustering.

Logic

Collect:

swingHighs

swingLows

Compute:

stdHigh = stddev(swingHighs)
stdLow  = stddev(swingLows)
normalizedHighSpread = stdHigh / totalRange
normalizedLowSpread  = stdLow  / totalRange


Low spread = tight boundary.

Scoring
boundaryScore = 1.0

if normalizedHighSpread < 0.15 → +0.05
if normalizedLowSpread  < 0.15 → +0.05

if either > 0.35 → multiply by 0.85


Cap at 1.1.

4.3 Alternation Purity
Purpose

Eliminate structural trend leakage.

Logic

Traverse swing sequence:

Detect:

higher-high progression

lower-low progression

Count violations:

progressionCount++


Compute:

progressionRatio = progressionCount / totalSwings

Scoring
if progressionRatio == 0 → 1.1
if < 0.2 → 1.0
if < 0.4 → 0.85
else → 0.7


Rationale:
Proper range alternates highs and lows without structural drift.

4.4 Width Preference (15m Optimized)
Purpose

Favor medium tradable width.

Logic
relativeWidth = totalRange / meanPrice


Suggested 15m band:

< 1% → too tight

2–6% → ideal

10% → too volatile

Scoring
if 0.02 ≤ width ≤ 0.06 → 1.1
if 0.01 ≤ width < 0.02 → 0.9
if 0.06 < width ≤ 0.10 → 0.9
else → 0.7


Soft only. No hard reject.

5. Final Formula
score = (1 - NDR)
        * RSS
        * ODS
        * travelScore
        * boundaryScore
        * alternationScore
        * widthScore


Clamp final score to [0, 1].

6. Backward Compatibility

Keep v1 available as:

sidewaysAlgo=v1

Introduce:

sidewaysAlgo=v4

No breaking changes.

7. Expected Behavioral Improvements

v4 should:

Stop ranking micro flatlines as top sideways

Stop favoring narrow noise boxes

Prioritize full-range oscillation structures

Visually align better with “lazy 15m tradable range”

Reduce sideways badge dominance

8. Performance Considerations

All new metrics:

O(n) over swings

No heavy regression

No percentile band recomputation

Negligible performance impact compared to candle fetching.

